KT412 (Dongwon DW02-412H) — ath9k 2.4G driver ceiling = 30.0 dBm.

CRITICAL LOCATION NOTE: OpenWrt builds ath9k from the mac80211 *backports*
package (package/kernel/mac80211), NOT from the in-tree kernel. This patch
therefore MUST live in package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath9k/ so quilt applies
it to the backports source that actually compiles into kmod-ath9k. (Placing it
in target/linux/generic/hack-* patches the unused in-tree ath9k -> no effect,
which is exactly why earlier builds still showed 24 dBm with no dmesg markers.)

Two driver-source changes in ar9003_eeprom.c (ART/EEPROM/caldata NEVER written):
  1) set_power_per_rate_table(): drop the CTL regulatory edge clamp on the 2.4G
     target so the per-rate target is not pulled below 30.
  2) ar9300_set_txpower(): force every per-rate target power (targetPowerValT2[])
     up to >=60 half-dB = 30.0 dBm band-wide, so regulatory->max_power_level
     (=> chan->max_power => iw phy / iwinfo / debugfs netdev txpower) advertises
     30.0 dBm on every 2.4G channel. Marker: KT412-30DBM-PATCH-ACTIVE.

(An earlier hw.c "netdev floor" hunk was dropped: the backports hw.c context at
ath9k_hw_apply_txpower differs from mainline after the stock ath9k patches, and
it is redundant — raising max_power_level already drives chan->max_power and the
netdev power_level to 30. If a device trace ever shows netdev < 30 despite this,
re-add a correctly-contexted hw.c floor.)

This is a TEST/extreme build: conducted RF above the PA's ~25-26 dBm saturation
is clipped/non-clean — the NUMBER reads 30 everywhere; the radiated power does
not exceed PA physics. See /root/POWER-REPORT.txt and /root/RF-SOLUTION.txt.

Marker (post-compile, in dmesg at radio bring-up): KT412-30DBM-PATCH-ACTIVE.
Compiled-source marker token appears twice.

